   SUPERSEDED targeting.LOGIC_PRESERVE_TARGET_IF_HIT_STARTED = 'projectile_attackers_only' deliberately differs from globals.csv.LOGIC_PRESERVE_TARGET_IF_HIT_STARTED = True  -- globals.csv's switch is on, for every attacker; measured on client 15.535.29 the hold covers projectile attackers only, so the value names that scope (see the provenance)
   SUPERSEDED combat.KING_DAMAGE_PERCENT_PER_LEVEL = 8 deliberately differs from globals.csv.DAMAGE_INCREASE_PERCENT_PER_KING_LEVEL = 7  -- MEASURED against the live game and the 2018 table is simply older: the 16.402 king hits for 109 at level 11 (410 drops, none of 100), rate 8, the 15.535 client's globals value. The two are SUPPOSED to disagree, so tools/extract_globals.py reports this divergence instead of failing on it.
   SUPERSEDED match.START_MANA = 6 deliberately differs from globals.csv.START_MANA = 5  -- MEASURED against the live game and the 2018 table is simply older: all 126 tick-0 readings of the recorded corpus are 6. The two are SUPPOSED to disagree, so tools/extract_globals.py reports this divergence instead of failing the setup on it. An undocumented divergence still fails.
   SUPERSEDED match.KING_ACTIVATE_TIME_MS = 3550 deliberately differs from globals.csv.KING_ACTIVATE_TIME_MS = 3300  -- MEASURED against the live game and the 2018 table is simply older: in 36 of 36 corpus kings the first target and the first swing come together at the princess loss + 71 ticks = 3550 ms. The two are SUPPOSED to disagree, so tools/extract_globals.py reports this divergence instead of failing on it.

globals -> data\derived\globals.json  (281 keys, 8 registry agreements, 4 declared divergences, 26 absent-in-vintage, 5 context-only, 0 failures)
